==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Giraffe Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Lion Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Normal Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Cow Cat is one of the fastest non-gacha cats you can have in the [[Empire of Cats]] Chapters. His speed means that he can easily rush to the frontlines to do some quick damage or block some hits for your ranged attackers when your meatshields get wiped out, but pay attention to your wallet!

Cow Cat can be effectively used to speedrun stages; with a high speed and attack rate, he can plow through weak enemies straight towards the enemy base. Using him with [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Gunslinger]] activates the [[Rawhide (Combo)|Rawhide]] [[Cat Combo]], further improving his speedrunning efficiency.

Early in the game, Cow Cat can be used to rush down weak [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies like [[Metal Hippoe]], as every non-[[Critical Hit|Critical]] attack does 1 damage, but don't expect this to work against anything stronger than [[Metal Doge]].

Cow Cat is a very good early game rusher, some new players can use him for finding treasures in early stages like in Empire of Cats. He cannot be used in [[Into the Future]] and further due to his low stats, especially notable on levels with strong enemies.

Cow Cat has 2 main weaknesses. Fast attacking and/or long ranged enemies, so be careful when using him against them.

==='''True Form'''===
In True Form, Lion Cat gains nearly double his original health and attack, at the cost of having a longer recharge time. Unfortunately, aside from the boosting of his stats, nothing else is changed. This means that Lion Cat remains outclassed by [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]], who has higher speed and Area Attack.

Even though he becomes outclassed by his Crazed and [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l]] variants for actual usage due to their special attributes and abilities, Lion Cat is nonetheless an important True Form to unlock because of his inclusion in [[Lion King (Combo)|Lion King]] and [[Three Kings (Combo)|Three Kings]], which most famously boost [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]]'s stats to [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] levels against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, as demonstrated against [[Hannya]] in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]].

